01	Display.Conversation	Notice	ODILE'S LOG, in an oilskin\Forty years I've cooked for the Wardens. Bread on the first day of the week, fish the rest. The cistern hums. The lake hums louder.\(The writing gets bigger, page by page.) It's warm in the water. I don't need the lamp. I hardly need to breathe.\(The last pages, in letters as tall as your hand.) THEY HEAR IT TOO, THE SAILORS. THEY COME DOWN THROUGH THE ROCK TO IT. I ONLY KEEP THEM FROM GOING TO IT. I'M SORRY. I'M SORRY ABOUT THE BOAT.	Close it.	02
